 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "commands is a list of space-separated strings; amounts are integer minor units. \"INIT <account> <balance>\" commands come first and create accounts. Timestamped commands follow in non-decreasing day order and are processed in input order. \"FUND <day> <account> <amount> <delay>\" is accepted when the account exists and settles on day + delay. \"BALANCE <day> <account>\" reports the settled balance at that point: the starting balance plus accepted funding settled by that day plus all earlier accepted balance changes, or -1 for an unknown account. Return the reported values in order. \"WITHDRAW <day> <account> <amount>\" is accepted when the account exists and amount does not exceed its settled balance at that point; it lowers the balance immediately. \"TRANSFER <day> <from> <to> <amount>\" is accepted when both accounts exist, they differ, and amount does not exceed the sender's settled balance; it moves the amount immediately as settled money.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
